### Basic Syntax (Elements and Attributes)

HTML uses elements and attributes to describe a page. Start by identifying the parts of an element.

<ExerciseCard question={getQuestion('html-parts')} />

Not all elements have the same structure. Next, consider an image.

<ExerciseCard question={getQuestion('img-void-element')} />

Elements can also contain other elements. Their nesting determines how the parts fit together.

<ExerciseCard question={getQuestion('overlapping-tags')} />

Finally, consider how formatting helps people read HTML.

